---
import Component from "../../layouts/Component.astro"
import Anatomy from "../../components/Anatomy.astro"
import AutoExample from "../../components/AutoExample.astro"
import Conditional from "../../components/Conditional.astro"
import DocLink from "../../components/DocLink.astro"
import PropOrClass from "../../components/PropOrClass.astro"
import { Rating as UIRating } from "@opui/astro"

import RatingCSS from "@opui/css/components/rating.css?raw"

import ratingApi from "../../component-api/rating/api"

export const description =
  "A star rating: a meter that shows a score, or radios that collect one."
---

<Component
  description={description}
  slug="rating"
  heroAnatomy
  apis={[{ title: "Rating API", api: ratingApi }]}
  browserSupport={[
    "attr",
    "container-style-queries",
    "has",
    "light-dark",
    "masks",
    "meter",
    "relative-color",
    "user-pseudos",
  ]}
  changelogPaths={[
    {
      path: "packages/opui/components/Rating/Rating.astro",
      type: "component",
    },
    { path: "src/docs/components/rating.astro", type: "docs" },
    { path: "src/component-examples/rating", type: "docs" },
    { path: "packages/opui/css/components/rating.css", type: "css" },
    { path: "src/component-api/rating", type: "api" },
  ]}
  installationTabs={[{ title: "rating.css", code: RatingCSS, lang: "css" }]}
>
  <Fragment slot="title">Rating</Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="preamble">
    A star rating. A <code>&lt;meter&gt;</code> shows a score, and a group of radios
    collects one. See also: <DocLink href="/components/radio" class="ui-link"
      >Radio</DocLink
    >, <DocLink href="/components/progress" class="ui-link">Progress</DocLink>.
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="anatomy">
    <Anatomy>
      <UIRating label="Your rating" name="anatomy-rating" value={3} />
    </Anatomy>
  </Fragment>

  <section>
    <h2 id="basics">Basics</h2>
    <Conditional as="p">
      <Fragment slot="astro"
        >Without <code>name</code>, a rating is a read-only <code
          >&lt;meter&gt;</code
        >. The <code>label</code> is its accessible name, so put the score in it.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="html"
        >Add <code>.ui-rating</code> to a <code>&lt;meter&gt;</code> with <code
          >max</code
        > and <code>value</code>. The <code>aria-label</code> is its accessible name,
        so put the score in it.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="svelte"
        >Without <code>name</code>, a rating is a read-only <code
          >&lt;meter&gt;</code
        >. The <code>label</code> is its accessible name, so put the score in it.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="vue"
        >Without <code>name</code>, a rating is a read-only <code
          >&lt;meter&gt;</code
        >. The <code>label</code> is its accessible name, so put the score in it.</Fragment
      >
    </Conditional>
    <AutoExample name="Basics" />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="input">Input</h2>
    <Conditional as="p">
      <Fragment slot="astro"
        >Set <code>name</code> to collect a rating. It renders a <code
          >&lt;fieldset&gt;</code
        > of radios, with the <code>label</code> as its legend.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="html"
        >Add <code>.ui-rating</code> to a <code>&lt;fieldset&gt;</code> with a <code
          >&lt;legend&gt;</code
        > and one radio per star, named with <code>aria-label</code>. The radio
        with <code>value="0"</code> clears the rating.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="svelte"
        >Set <code>name</code> to collect a rating. It renders a <code
          >&lt;fieldset&gt;</code
        > of radios, with the <code>label</code> as its legend. Bind the rating with
        <code>bind:value</code>.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="vue"
        >Set <code>name</code> to collect a rating. It renders a <code
          >&lt;fieldset&gt;</code
        > of radios, with the <code>label</code> as its legend. Bind the rating with
        <code>v-model</code>.</Fragment
      >
    </Conditional>
    <p>
      Hovering previews a rating, and a click or the arrow keys set it. The icon
      before the stars clears it, and stays visible so touch users can find it.
      The count after the stars is a CSS counter. Browsers without <code
        >:has()</code
      > only fill the checked star.
    </p>
    <AutoExample name="Input" />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="sizes">Sizes</h2>
    <p>
      Resize a rating with <PropOrClass prop='size="small"' class=".ui-small" /> or
      <PropOrClass prop='size="large"' class=".ui-large" />. Input stars are
      bigger than meter stars, so each radio stays at least 24px wide.
    </p>
    <AutoExample name="Sizes" row />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="fractions">Fractions</h2>
    <p>
      The meter fills the exact fraction, so 4.9 doesn't round up to five stars.
    </p>
    <AutoExample name="Fractions" column />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="max">Max</h2>
    <Conditional as="p">
      <Fragment slot="astro"
        ><code>max</code> sets the number of stars. Defaults to <code>5</code
        >.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="html"
        ><code>max</code> sets the number of stars, read with typed <code
          >attr()</code
        >. Browsers without it need <code>--_max</code> with the same number, or they
        draw five stars.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="svelte"
        ><code>max</code> sets the number of stars. Defaults to <code>5</code
        >.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="vue"
        ><code>max</code> sets the number of stars. Defaults to <code>5</code
        >.</Fragment
      >
    </Conditional>
    <AutoExample name="Max" column />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="disabled">Disabled</h2>
    <p>
      Set <code>disabled</code> to disable every radio.
    </p>
    <AutoExample name="Disabled" />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="validation">Validation</h2>
    <Conditional as="p">
      <Fragment slot="astro"
        ><code>required</code> drops the no rating radio, so a star has to be picked.
        <code>error</code> marks the radios invalid and tints the empty stars. Point
        <code>aria-describedby</code> at the error message.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="html"
        >Set <code>required</code> on the radios and leave out the no rating radio,
        so a star has to be picked. <code>aria-invalid="true"</code> on the radios
        tints the empty stars. Point <code>aria-describedby</code> at the error message.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="svelte"
        ><code>required</code> drops the no rating radio, so a star has to be picked.
        <code>error</code> marks the radios invalid and tints the empty stars. Point
        <code>aria-describedby</code> at the error message.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="vue"
        ><code>required</code> drops the no rating radio, so a star has to be picked.
        <code>error</code> marks the radios invalid and tints the empty stars. Point
        <code>aria-describedby</code> at the error message.</Fragment
      >
    </Conditional>
    <AutoExample name="Validation" />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="localization">Localization</h2>
    <p>
      In right-to-left text the meter fills from the right, and the radios and
      arrow keys follow the reading direction.
    </p>
    <Conditional as="p">
      <Fragment slot="astro"
        >The radios are named "No rating", "1 star", "2 stars" and so on.
        Translate them with <code>clearLabel</code> and <code>starLabel</code>,
        a function that gets the star's value. Use <code>Intl.PluralRules</code> for
        languages with more plural forms.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="html"
        >Translate the <code>aria-label</code> of each radio.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="svelte"
        >The radios are named "No rating", "1 star", "2 stars" and so on.
        Translate them with <code>clearLabel</code> and <code>starLabel</code>,
        a function that gets the star's value. Use <code>Intl.PluralRules</code> for
        languages with more plural forms.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="vue"
        >The radios are named "No rating", "1 star", "2 stars" and so on.
        Translate them with <code>clearLabel</code> and <code>starLabel</code>,
        a function that gets the star's value. Use <code>Intl.PluralRules</code> for
        languages with more plural forms.</Fragment
      >
    </Conditional>
    <AutoExample name="Localization" />
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="accessibility">
    <p>
      The meter is announced with its label and value. Screen readers may read
      the value as a percentage, so put the score in the label, such as "Rated
      4.5 out of 5".
    </p>
    <p>
      The input is a group of native radios named by the legend. Each radio has
      its own name, such as "3 stars", and the arrow keys move between them. The
      count after the stars is hidden from screen readers, since the checked
      radio already says it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Radios get the library's focus ring. Each input star is at least 24px
      wide. In forced colors mode filled stars use <code>SelectedItem</code> on the
      input and <code>CanvasText</code> on the meter, and empty stars use <code
        >GrayText</code
      >.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</Component>
